Z||000000||Oreif||08-13-2001||12:04 PM||||Hey All,<BR>A friend has a 1984 Jeep Larado. The Jeep was in mint condition with very low miles and his son bumped the driverside door. The door is fixed but the decal that says "Larado" for the doors needs to be put back on. Jeep no longer sells them and the aftermarket ones are not exact. So if anyone has or knows where I could find an Original decal set in the silver/black (2-color) letters please Email me. <BR>Thanks,<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||08-13-2001||12:21 PM||||Have your dealer do a distribution/warehouse check to see if it locates any NOS stripes. Sometimes you can run across some left overs somewhere. I just got some obsolete parts for a LeBaron that are no longer available. If not you may have to go with aftermarket and do one whole side, or both. An alternative would be a place that makes vinyl graphics and take a pic of the good side and have them cut a replacement for you. that should be ez since you dont have any wierd colors.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Leadfoot||08-13-2001||12:31 PM||||I think you can get decals for jeeps at<BR> <A HREF="http://www.quadratec.com" TARGET=_blank>www.quadratec.com</A> <BR>I buy all my jeep stuff there.  If not, there are so many jeep accessory stores on the web it's not funny. <p>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 08-13-2001).]||||reg||1
